%% Sequence — Login with Google, OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code flow (report sequence 4)
%% Based on seq-google-login.mmd by Thulani Jayathilake (Role 2); corrected against docs/architecture.md v1.2 §6.1, §9, §10.4
%% Changes: browser traffic goes through the gateway; Spring's default OAuth paths (/oauth2/**, /login/oauth2/**) are
%% forwarded to auth-service unchanged, without the /api/v1 prefix (team decision, 31 Oct 2026); error branches;
%% first API call with the JWT. Google login is switched on with AUTH_GOOGLE_ENABLED=true.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Customer
    participant SPA as React SPA (browser)
    participant GW as api-gateway :8080
    participant AUTH as auth-service :8081
    participant DB as auth_db
    participant G as Google OAuth 2.0

    User->>SPA: click "Continue with Google"
    SPA->>GW: GET /oauth2/authorization/google (public, no /api/v1 prefix)
    GW->>AUTH: forward unchanged
    AUTH-->>SPA: 302 to Google authorize URL<br/>(client_id, scope openid email profile, state, redirect_uri)
    SPA->>G: sign in and consent
    alt user cancels or denies
        G-->>SPA: 302 /login/oauth2/code/google?error=access_denied
        SPA->>GW: GET /login/oauth2/code/google?error=…
        GW->>AUTH: forward unchanged
        AUTH-->>SPA: 302 SPA /auth/callback?error=…
    else consent given
        G-->>SPA: 302 /login/oauth2/code/google?code&state
        SPA->>GW: GET /login/oauth2/code/google?code&state
        GW->>AUTH: forward unchanged
        AUTH->>AUTH: check state (CSRF)
        AUTH->>G: POST token endpoint (code + client secret), back channel
        G-->>AUTH: ID token (sub, email, name, email_verified)
        AUTH->>DB: find oauth_accounts (GOOGLE, sub)<br/>else link by verified email, else create user + CUSTOMER role
        AUTH->>DB: INSERT oauth_login_codes (SHA-256 hash, expires in 2 min)
        AUTH-->>SPA: 302 SPA /auth/callback?code=<one-time code>
        SPA->>GW: POST /api/v1/auth/token {code} (public route)
        GW->>AUTH: forward
        AUTH->>DB: lock code row, check unexpired and unused, set consumed_at
        alt code unknown, expired or already used
            AUTH-->>SPA: 400 ProblemDetail (via GW)
        else valid
            AUTH->>DB: INSERT refresh_tokens (SHA-256 hash, 7 days)
            AUTH-->>SPA: 200 {accessToken RS256 15 min with roles claim, refreshToken, user} (via GW)
        end
    end

    Note over SPA,AUTH: later requests
    SPA->>GW: GET /api/v1/parcels · Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
    GW->>GW: verify signature with cached JWKS (auth-service /.well-known/jwks.json, internal)
    GW->>GW: route to parcel-service, which verifies the JWT again and checks @PreAuthorize
